>> title: Sablé Cookies
>> category: Cookies
>> tags: butter, french, slice and bake, teatime, oven
>> counters: Bakery
>> aka: sablés, sables, French butter cookies
>> servings: 30
>> time: 3 hours
>> slack: narrow — eighteen minutes takes them to the pale gold a sablé wants, and the butter browns fast after that

Heat the #oven{} to 350°F (175°C) and line two #baking sheets{} with parchment.

Cream @unsalted butter{1%cup}(226 g; softened) with @powdered sugar{2/3%cup}(80 g).

>> step: beat in
Beat @egg yolk{1}(18 g) and @vanilla extract{1%tsp}(5 mL) into @&(~1)creamed butter{}.

Whisk @all-purpose flour{2%cup}(250 g) and @fine sea salt{1/2%tsp}(3 g).

Stir @&(~1)dry ingredients{} into @&(~2)batter{}.

Roll @&(~1)dough{} into a log and chill for ~{2%hours}.

>> step: egg wash, roll edges in sugar, slice 1/2 in, bake 350°F (175°C) 18 min
Brush @&(~1)log{} with @beaten egg yolk{1}(18 g), roll the edges in @turbinado sugar{1/4%cup}(50 g), slice 1/2 in thick, and bake at 350°F for ~{18%min}.
